{"name":"Secret Garden","hex":"#11aa66","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"secret","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of knowledge that is hidden and intended to be kept hidden. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The key or principle by which something is made clear; the knack."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep secret.","To hide secretly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Secret Garden","blocks":[{"text":"The Secret Garden is a children's novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett first published in book form in 1911, after serialisation in The American Magazine. Set in England, it is seen as a classic of English children's literature. The American edition was published by the Frederick A. Stokes Company with illustrations by M. L. Kirk, and the British edition by Heinemann with illustrations by Charles Robinson. Several stage and film adaptations have been made of The Secret Garden."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg/330px-Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Secret_Garden","wikidata":"Q472194"},{"title":"The Secret Garden (1918 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Secret Garden is a lost 1918 American drama silent film directed by Gustav von Seyffertitz and written by Frances Hodgson Burnett and Marion Fairfax. The film stars Lila Lee, Spottiswoode Aitken, Clarence Geldart, Richard Rosson, Fay Holderness and Ann Malone. The film was released by Paramount Pictures on January 12, 1919, after December 1918 premieres in Oklahoma City and New York City."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Secret_Garden_lobby_card.jpg/330px-Secret_Garden_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Secret_Garden_(1918_film)","wikidata":"Q17479192"},{"title":"Secret Garden (South Korean TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Secret Garden is a 2010 South Korean television drama starring Ha Ji-won, Hyun Bin, Yoon Sang-hyun, and Kim Sa-rang. It aired on SBS from November 13, 2010 to January 16, 2011, on Saturdays and Sundays at 22:00 (KST) for 20 episodes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/Secret_garden_korean_drama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secret_Garden_(South_Korean_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q45871"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg/500px-Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg/1280px-Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg/500px-Houghton_AC85_B9345_911s_-_Secret_Garden%2C_1911_-_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","l